  "notes": [
    "Document entries are placeholders for operator-provided UTF-8 text extracted from PDFs/EPUBs; create those .tmp files locally before running the collector.",
    "Repository commands are intentionally limited to read-only git operations by scripts/headroom_corpus_collect.py.",
    "Generated samples, fixtures, cloned repositories, PDFs, EPUBs, and extracted text stay under .tmp/headroom and must not be committed.",
    "Project Gutenberg/Gutendex are recommended public-domain prose sources; download bounded UTF-8 TXT/EPUB-derived text into .tmp/headroom/sources/ and use optional document entries.",
    "arXiv is useful for technical PDF-like prose, but use manually selected/extracted UTF-8 text samples rather than bulk S3/Kaggle downloads.",
    "GitHub events/GH Archive style JSON should be sampled or synthesized in bounded form; do not require bulk public-event datasets for local eval."
  ]
